speechtext:
(c) subject to the provisions of this section the redemption of preference or preferred shares, heretofore or hereafter issued by the company, may be effected in accordance with the terms on which such shares are or have been issued by the company;
That is enabling legislation, of course, and at the moment I do not just visualize what the implications may 'be. You cannot predicate a judgment on this whole question unless you know the terms under which these shares were originally issued, and we have not had it.
Then section 6 deals with the enabling provisions of seotion 3, to which I have already referred. I would have thought, in drafting this measure that would have been the first section in the bill, but apparently the draftsman did not think so.
